This product bundles the following third-party components:

- PyMuPDF  (https://github.com/pymupdf/PyMuPDF)
    License: GNU AGPL-3.0
    A Python binding for MuPDF (© Artifex Software, Inc.). Because PyMuPDF is
    AGPL-3.0, this combined work is distributed under AGPL-3.0.

- pymupdfb
    License: GNU AGPL-3.0
    The native MuPDF binaries shipped alongside PyMuPDF.

- PySide6 / Qt for Python  (https://www.qt.io/qt-for-python)
    License: GNU LGPL-3.0
    Qt is © The Qt Company Ltd and other contributors.

- qt-material  (https://github.com/dunderlab/qt-material)
    License: BSD-2-Clause
    Material-design stylesheet for Qt applications; provides the app theme.
    Bundles the Roboto font family (Apache-2.0).

- Jinja2 / MarkupSafe  (https://palletsprojects.com/)
    License: BSD-3-Clause
    Template engine used by qt-material (transitive dependencies, bundled in
    the frozen build).

- QtAwesome  (https://github.com/spyder-ide/qtawesome)
    License: MIT
    Icon fonts for Qt applications; provides the app's icon set. Bundles
    icon fonts under their own licences, including Material Design Icons
    (Apache-2.0, the set this app uses), Font Awesome (SIL OFL 1.1),
    Elusive Icons (SIL OFL 1.1), Phosphor (MIT), Remix Icon (Apache-2.0)
    and Microsoft Codicons (CC BY 4.0).

- QtPy  (https://github.com/spyder-ide/qtpy)
    License: MIT
    Qt-binding abstraction used by QtAwesome (transitive dependency,
    bundled in the frozen build).

- pytesseract  (https://github.com/madmaze/pytesseract)
    License: Apache-2.0
    Python wrapper used for OCR text extraction; invokes the external
    Tesseract OCR engine as a subprocess.

- Pillow  (https://python-pillow.github.io/)
    License: MIT-CMU
    Imaging library used to hand rendered pages to the OCR engine, and by
    pyHanko to render image signature appearances.

- pyHanko  (https://github.com/MatthiasValvekens/pyHanko)
    License: MIT
    Cryptographic PDF signing library — appends digital signatures to
    finished documents as incremental updates. Ships some PyPDF2-derived
    code under its included LICENSE.PyPDF2 (BSD-3-Clause-style).

- pyhanko-certvalidator  (https://github.com/MatthiasValvekens/certvalidator)
    License: MIT
    X.509 certificate path validation used by pyHanko (transitive
    dependency, bundled in the frozen build).

- asn1crypto  (https://github.com/wbond/asn1crypto)
    License: MIT
    ASN.1 parsing/serialisation used by pyHanko (transitive dependency).

- oscrypto  (https://github.com/wbond/oscrypto)
    License: MIT
    OS-backed crypto primitives used by pyhanko-certvalidator (transitive
    dependency).

- uritools  (https://github.com/tkem/uritools)
    License: MIT
    RFC 3986 URI parsing used by pyhanko-certvalidator (transitive
    dependency).

- cryptography  (https://cryptography.io/)
    License: Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause
    Cryptographic primitives: loads PKCS#12 certificate bundles and
    generates the optional self-signed signing certificates. Binds OpenSSL
    (Apache-2.0) via cffi (MIT) and pycparser (BSD-3-Clause).

- requests  (https://requests.readthedocs.io/)
    License: Apache-2.0
    HTTP client required by pyHanko (transitive dependency; used for
    optional online validation/timestamping, which this app does not do).
    Brings certifi (MPL-2.0), urllib3 (MIT), charset-normalizer (MIT) and
    idna (BSD-3-Clause).

- PyYAML  (https://pyyaml.org/)
    License: MIT
    YAML parsing required by pyHanko's configuration layer (transitive
    dependency; unused at runtime by this app).

- lxml  (https://lxml.de/)
    License: BSD-3-Clause
    XML tooling required by pyHanko (transitive dependency); binds libxml2
    and libxslt (MIT-style licences).

- tzlocal  (https://github.com/regebro/tzlocal)
    License: MIT
    Local-timezone lookup used by pyHanko for signing timestamps; brings
    tzdata (Apache-2.0, IANA time-zone data).

- python-barcode  (https://github.com/WhyNotHugo/python-barcode)
    License: MIT
    Barcode rendering pulled in by pyHanko's image-support extra (unused at
    runtime by this app).

- Tesseract OCR  (https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract)
    License: Apache-2.0
    The OCR engine itself — an external program, not a Python package.
    Packaged builds bundle the Windows runtime (UB-Mannheim build
    5.4.0.20240606): tesseract.exe, libtesseract, and the English model
    data (eng.traineddata, tessdata_fast — Apache-2.0) as application
    assets; development machines use a local installation instead.
    The bundled runtime's third-party libraries (its verified dependency
    closure) and their licences:
      Leptonica (Leptonica License, BSD-2-Clause-style); libjpeg-turbo
      (IJG + BSD + zlib); libpng (PNG Reference Library licence); libtiff
      (libtiff/MIT-style licence); zlib; libdeflate (MIT); libwebp and
      libsharpyuv (BSD-3-Clause); giflib (MIT); OpenJPEG (BSD-2-Clause);
      LERC (Apache-2.0); jbigkit (GPL-2.0-or-later — verified wording;
      compatible with this product's AGPL-3.0); libarchive (BSD-2-Clause);
      OpenSSL libcrypto 3 (Apache-2.0); xz / liblzma (0BSD); bzip2
      (BSD-style); lz4 (BSD-2-Clause); zstd (BSD-3-Clause); BLAKE2 libb2
      (CC0); expat (MIT); GNU libiconv (LGPL-2.1-or-later, dynamically
      linked); MinGW-w64 runtime — libstdc++/libgcc (GPL-3.0 WITH GCC
      Runtime Library Exception) and libwinpthread (MIT/BSD-style).
    The installer's training tools and their UI/text-rendering stack
    (ICU, GLib, Pango, Cairo, fontconfig, FreeType, HarfBuzz, …) are NOT
    bundled.

